        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Both ACE inhibitors and ARBs (angiotensin receptor blockers) are equally effective first-line treatments for high blood pressure, but ARBs are generally preferred for tolerability because they have a significantly lower risk of causing a persistent dry cough or angioedema.",
